# Week 02 Class Project

## Purpose

This program calculates electrical current using voltage and resistance.
It also checks that the input is valid and that resistance is greater than zero.

## Input Format

The program expects two numbers separated by whitespace:

EX: 12 4

## Build and Run Commands

Build: g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic src/main.cpp -o build/app
Run: ./build/app

## Example Output 

Current: 3 A

## Limitations

This program only calculates current from a voltage and a resistance. It does not perform unit conversions and the resistance must be greater than zero. It also does not check for realistic values.

## Debugging Reflection

There was an issue when testing where the output did not match the expected output. There was a letter capitalized in the expected output when it should have been lowercase. Fixing this made the program work.